      "content": "Immediate steps: Evacuate the refrigerated area and isolate the non-hazardous items. Disconnect the engine and switch to backup power or divert to a nearby cooler (if available) to keep perishables cool. Notify dispatch and have a backup truck or insulated railroad container ready to transfer or store the cargo. \n\nFood safety protocols: Check if the failed unit caused the temperature to rise above 40°F (4°C) for an extended period. Inspect the tuna for signs of spoilage, such as sliminess, off-odors, or discoloration. Document all actions taken and contact local health authorities if necessary for guidance. Ensure that crew members handling the tuna wear proper gloves and sanitation procedures are followed.",
