      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sudden unit failure without a clear mechanical or electrical cause can be due to various factors, including a manufacturing defect, a software issue, or environmental factors that weren't previously known. Another possibility is a \" micro-surge\" or transients in the electrical system, which might have caused an intermittent failure. Witnessing unusual usage patterns or exposure to unusual power conditions, such as a voltage spike, can also lead to such sudden failures without any physical signs of damage.",
